       "id": "v2-proposal-j25-030502-j25-q-a",
       "type": "part",
       "label": "a",
       "prompt": "Use the discriminant to show that $2x^2+x+5=0$ has no real solutions.",
       "answerSpaceMm": 30,
       "answer": {
        "short": "$\\Delta=-39<0$, so there are no real solutions.",
        "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=b^2-4ac\\\\&=1^2-4(2)(5)\\\\&=-39\\end{align*}$$ Since $\\Delta<0$, there are no real solutions."
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "v2-proposal-j25-030502-j25-q-b",
       "type": "part",
       "label": "b",
       "prompt": "Solve $x^2-6x+4=0$, expressing your answers in exact form.",
       "answerSpaceMm": 40,
       "answer": {
        "short": "$x=3\\pm\\sqrt{5}$",
        "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\\\\&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt{36-16}}{2}\\\\&=\\frac{6\\pm2\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\\\&=3\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\end{align*}$$"
       }
      }
     ],
